    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n56903" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κερο-βάτης</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾰ], <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>, ὁ,
			</span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κέρας</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>horn-footed, hoofed</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κεροβάτας Πάν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Ra.</u>
					230
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.): acc. to some Gramm., <i>he that goes with
			horns</i>, i.e. <i>the horned god</i>; acc. to Sch., <i>he that
				walks the mountain-peaks</i> (cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κέρας</span> v.<i><span class="en">
				6
			</span></i>).</div>
